  "behavior": [
    "Facade capture/restore/fork acquire fresh host authority before copied metadata, IDs, parser/cursor and delivery state.",
    "Neutral snapshot driver independently acquires after pure identity/known-estimate checks and before owned discovery/estimator construction, logical reservation or any controller/capture/native copy.",
    "HostPreparation errors preserve typed BackendFailure causes without treating rejected acquisition as native failure or consuming the logical copy ledger.",
    "Core continuation retains combined source/destination custody; restore attaches before installation and keeps a local clone through displaced payload cleanup.",
    "Facade snapshot/session/branch authority is last and moves with host state on exchange. Initial semantic sessions inherit existing parser authority for enclosing payload destruction.",
    "Capture identity owner shares payload-free custody across preexisting checkpoint/partition handles. Payload-first field ordering and unlock-before-erased-drop preserve retirement and reentry.",
    "Forked captures preserve distinct identities with inherited source custody. Speculative activation checkpoints retain capture host custody without changing their control identity.",
    "Actual controller-copy counters and host/native callback counters stay unchanged after rejected direct neutral capture/restore/fork admission."
